{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>His enemies.</b> Meaning, Edom and Seir. And the verse's saying <b>he will possess</b> means: it shall never be rebuilt again and they shall have no revival, unlike the other nations who will survive through them, as stated. And He gave the reason: because they are the enemies of Israel, as it is written (Psalms 137:7): ״זְכֹר ה׳ לִבְנֵי אֱדוֹם״ and so forth; therefore their punishment is greater than that of all the children of Shet." "<b>And Israel is doing valiantly.</b> Meaning, in the midst of the destruction of Edom and the other children of Shet, Israel will do valiantly. That is to say, that which the Samael and the other nations had swallowed, they [Israel] will extract from his mouth. And since the holy sparks are defiled while they are within the klipah, when they are refined and emerge from it they are mended — therefore it says <b>doing valiantly</b>, in the sense of mending the valor that had been swallowed within them."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:59.372258358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}